From: mojavemesa-lgtm <252102886+mojavemesa-lgtm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Bluetooth: use the WCN3990 offload data path for eSCO

Mark WCN3990 with QCA_CAP_HFP_HW_OFFLOAD and, when userspace gives no data path
(PulseAudio 17 does not), default the enhanced eSCO setup to the controller
offload path, so SCO goes over SLIMbus instead of HCI (the WCN3990 firmware
never sends SCO over HCI). The hci_conn.c part is a hack; a proper version
probably belongs in userspace or a per-controller default. Note: setting
transport_unit_size to 0 (as Android does) BROKE audio for us; keep 16.

Tested on OnePlus 6T (fajita) with wcn3990-bluetooth-hfp-v4 on 7.1-rc1.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -2135,6 +2135,8 @@
 
 static const struct qca_device_data qca_soc_data_wcn3990 __maybe_unused = {
 	.soc_type = QCA_WCN3990,
+	/* SCO audio goes over SLIMbus to the ADSP, never over HCI */
+	.capabilities = QCA_CAP_HFP_HW_OFFLOAD,
 	.vregs = (struct qca_vreg []) {
 		{ "vddio", 15000  },
 		{ "vddxo", 80000  },
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
@@ -295,6 +295,13 @@
 
 	configure_datapath_sync(hdev, &conn->codec);
 
+	/* No data path from userspace: use the controller's offload (non-HCI) path if it has one */
+	if (!conn->codec.data_path && hdev->get_data_path_id) {
+		__u8 dp = 0;
+		if (!hdev->get_data_path_id(hdev, &dp))
+			conn->codec.data_path = dp;
+	}
+
 	conn->state = BT_CONNECT;
 	conn->out = true;
 
